2. WHICH SIGN BRANCH.  The solve returns |theta_ped|, so +theta and -theta
   fit identically; continuity permits only the two global branches below.
   TEST: any causal H = (minimum-phase) x (all-pass), and an all-pass's
   phase is MONOTONICALLY NON-INCREASING in f.  So
        excess(f) = arg(H) - phi_minphase(f)
   must be non-increasing.  A rising excess is impossible for ANY causal
   LTI element, whatever its order.

