4. IDENTIFYING THE BLEED LEVEL FROM CAUSALITY.
   The solve fits (s, theta) per band at a GIVEN beta, and beta is the
   parameter session 31 left unresolved at +/-2 dB. It is not innocent:
   raising beta by 2.6 dB moves the required extra phase at 254 Hz from
   +38 to +120 deg. So beta and the missing element are COUPLED and cannot
   be settled one at a time -- which is why 'fit the phase first, the level
   later' has no fixed point.
   But magnitude and phase are not independent for a causal element, and
   THAT is an equation the levels alone do not provide. Scan beta; at each
   one fit a minimum-phase rational to |G| and ask how far its phase falls
   short. The beta where a causal element can actually do the job is the
   physically admissible one.

