   driveRMS = how well that beta explains the 5-point DRIVE SWEEP at all
              12 core bands (the evidence that identifies s and theta).
   edge     = how many of those 12 had theta pin at 0 or 180, i.e. a
              DEGENERATE solve; those are excluded from the columns right
              of it, so a low beta is scored on fewer real measurements.
   mean/worst/shortRMS = how far a minimum-phase element falls short of the
              lead the captures demand. Negative is impossible for ANY causal
              element -- non-minimum-phase content only subtracts phase.

   READ THIS TABLE AS A DISAGREEMENT, NOT AS A FIT. driveRMS is minimised
   near beta = -15.5 and causality wants beta <= -18.5; they pull opposite
   ways. And shortRMS never falls below ~28 deg ANYWHERE, so no beta makes
   the requirement cleanly realisable -- at best the mean crosses zero while
   individual bands stay +/-30-50 deg out. That is not a candidate.

