   40-101 Hz sits at 2-5 dB regardless of beta. That is session 31 item 6:
   the model's mu_d PEAKS at drive 2:30 and falls by max, while the pedal's
   must grow monotonically straight through the null. The solve fits (s,
   theta) against that wrong drive shape, so the phase target inherits it
   exactly where A3 lives.

   beta with the mean shortfall within 15 deg of 0: -21.0, -20.0, -19.5, -19.0, -18.5
   Model bleed is -16.93 dB, so causality leans toward the model's bleed being
   ~2.1 dB HIGHER than the pedal's -- the SIGN session 29 measured directly from
   the drive-min LF total (-17.4..-18.3 dB), and the OPPOSITE of the session-31
   least-squares (-15.2). Do not promote this to a measurement: it leans on
   bands whose theta is pinned at 180, and driveRMS moves only 1.84 -> 2.10 dB
   across the whole range, so the least-squares was never strong evidence
   either. What is settled is that the bleed level is STILL open, and that it
   cannot be settled after the phase, because the phase target depends on it.

